(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #103: a text field is an ordinary expression and
 lvalue. Through a quoted name, a bare `is`, a member maker, a text
 parameter, a list append (which keeps the value it was given), a
 comparison with a literal, interpolation, and a text variable that
 outlives the field's next write.)

A thing called note has
  a function called 'signed by',
  a text called body is "hello",
  a text called title.

To do the note's 'signed by', with a text called author.
  a note called signed.
  Set signed's title to author.
  Return a note, signed.

To shouted with a text called word.
  Return a text, "{word}!".

To 'title of' with a note called given.
  Return a text, given's title.

Create a note called 'the first'.
'the first''s title is "set with a bare is".
Print 'the first''s title.
If 'the first''s body is "hello" then,
  Print "the body is hello".
Print shouted of 'the first''s body.
a list called kept is [].
append 'the first''s title to kept.
Set 'the first''s title to "changed after the append".
Print kept.
a text called local is 'the first''s body.
Set 'the first''s body to "".
Print local.
Print "body [{'the first''s body}], title [{'the first''s title}]".
The made is a note's 'signed by' with "Grace".
Print made.
Print 'title of' of made.
Print 'the first''s 'title of'.
